WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.010
- We're in the middle of our first ever

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.320
Designed By Drew segment,

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.690
where I get to surprise
this very special family

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.530
of five essential workers with
a backyard transformation.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.423
Check this out, they have no
idea what's about to happen.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.950
I'm so excited, I love surprises!

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.340
The Copenings have no
idea this is happening.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.520
The team was able to pull
this off in five hours.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:27.660
Behind their backs, we
plotted and schemed.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.113
And yay, I hope they like it so much.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.560
I really wanna thank our friends at Weber.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.053
They were kind enough to gift

00:00:37.053 --> 00:00:40.830
the Weber Genesis to the Copening family.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:44.890
And Ooni, they're a pizza oven
company, they kindly donated

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:49.190
this beautiful outdoor pizza
oven and this entire stand.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.160
I'd like to give a special
shout out to Tyson as well,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.270
because they've gifted the
Copenings groceries for the year.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.740
SYNLawn donated the grass.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.050
Then we also were able to
work with Pottery Barn.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:06.800
And they were able to give
us these amazing table

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.930
and chairs and this gorgeous couch.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.270
And we talked about should we do something

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.610
really colorful for the Copenings?

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:19.610
And my design aesthetic is
usually very color-forward,

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.936
But lately, because of
the state of the world,

00:01:21.936 --> 00:01:25.560
it's so chaotic out there
that I keep wanting to create

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.040
spaces that are very
calm and very neutral,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.850
and don't maximize more than three colors.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.730
I'm really happy with the end result.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.423
And I hope they like it too.

00:01:37.582 --> 00:01:40.653
- Okay, I think they're
here, I'll be right back.

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:48.886
- Oh my god!
- Oh!

00:01:50.488 --> 00:01:53.238
(family cheers)

00:01:55.743 --> 00:01:58.113
I wanna be adopted into your family.

00:01:59.405 --> 00:02:00.238
- Oh you got it, Drew,

00:02:00.238 --> 00:02:01.680
you come right in front of Mike, Mike.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.280
- And Shakia, you're like
the queen entertainer.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.240
- Yes.
- You bring the games

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.250
and the karaoke.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.453
So I brought some like games for you.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:15.360
I brought some grilling
books for you, Papa Mike.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.040
I know you're the grill master.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.020
- Yes.
- I am so happy

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.423
to be in your backyard.

00:02:23.037 --> 00:02:26.109
I'm your boo Drew, and I'm trespassing.

00:02:26.109 --> 00:02:26.990
(family laughs)

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:29.443
Come sit down, relax in your new patio,

00:02:30.415 --> 00:02:31.720
your new beautiful backyard?

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.607
Okay.
- This is beautiful.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.350
- Why us?

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:41.053
Like, I'm excited that
it's us, but I'm like, us?

00:02:41.053 --> 00:02:42.384
- Can I just ask one thing?

00:02:42.384 --> 00:02:43.220
Can we just keep this yard?

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.561
This yard is beautiful.

00:02:44.561 --> 00:02:47.053
- We love this yard!

00:02:47.053 --> 00:02:48.747
- This is all yours.
- Wow.

00:02:48.747 --> 00:02:50.750
Nothing's going anywhere.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.360
- Oh my god, I love it, I love it.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.480
- I can't decide who does
a more important job.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.470
And the world is in a different space,

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.040
where it has a new name, essential.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.670
There are new capes, there's
respect, there's heroes.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:11.520
And for that, I'm so grateful
for what you guys do.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.200
And so we wanted to show you

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.972
our appreciation by hooking ya up.

00:03:17.972 --> 00:03:20.820
(family cheers)

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:25.520
How was it working in assisted
living during coronavirus?

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.650
Did it change you as a person

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:32.459
to be a part of so much of passing on?

00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:34.790
- Yes, it changed me, definitely.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.920
Even though me and my family
were close, we got closer,

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.010
because you really got to
understand who you can depend on.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:45.825
- To just like still be able
to come home and have our unit

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:49.100
be safe, be healthy and be in a place

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.730
where we can still like
celebrate and enjoy each other.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.680
- You work at the MTA?
- Yes.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.412
- And Papa Mike, you work at the MTA?

00:03:57.412 --> 00:03:58.245
- Yes.

00:03:58.245 --> 00:04:00.090
- [Drew] And you are at the post office.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.280
- Yes, 24 years.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.470
- Mail is so important.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.461
- Yes it is.

00:04:05.461 --> 00:04:07.290
- What you do is so important.
- Thank you.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:09.150
- I'm like one of your biggest fans.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.890
- Thank you, I'm glad to know.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.903
Did y'all hear that, bus operators?

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.910
- Teachers too.
- That's right!

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:18.067
And you're a teacher!
- Yes.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:23.100
- My favorite thing, obviously
there's so much work to do,

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:28.100
but the fact that 2020 has
doctors and nurses and teachers

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.870
and bus drivers and the
post office and everything,

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.840
may we never, ever, ever not be

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.503
in the lane we are in right now.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.822
So thank you.

00:04:40.822 --> 00:04:41.655
- And if I had to, Drew,
I would do it all again.

00:04:41.655 --> 00:04:42.946
- Thank you, Drew.
- Yes.

00:04:42.946 --> 00:04:45.050
Thank you.
- I would do it all again.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.630
- I Love you so much it hurts!

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.710
- We love you.
- Love you.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:54.710
- I cannot thank you guys enough
for having me in your home.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.920
That's your family home
that you grew up in.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:04:59.753
- Yeah.

00:04:59.753 --> 00:05:02.550
- And you're keeping it going
by raising your own kids here.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:05.352
Well, I wish I could hug you guys.

00:05:05.352 --> 00:05:06.699
- I wish I could squeeze you, Drew.

00:05:06.699 --> 00:05:11.699
- I want a group hug,
soon, when it's safe.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.084
- That was amazing.

00:05:15.084 --> 00:05:15.917
- That was incredible.

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:18.216
- That was, oh my god.

00:05:18.216 --> 00:05:19.560
- I did not expect that at all.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.803
- I didn't expect that at all.
- No.

00:05:20.803 --> 00:05:23.990
This is the best day of the year.

00:05:24.826 --> 00:05:25.667
- [All] Thank you Drew.

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:28.113
- We love you you so much, we love you!

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.370
- What a wonderful family.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:37.070
We thank you for all that you do.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:40.340
And to you watching, do you
have a space that needs help,

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:43.290
or know someone who
deserves a special surprise?

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:46.505
Please go to our website
and tell me all about it.

00:05:46.505 --> 00:05:49.088
(upbeat music)

